    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Progressive weakness and loss of coordination for about a year: fumbling with buttons and a bat, tripping on curbs, a fall on the ice in the winter, muscle cramps and twitching in the arms and thighs; no numbness, pain, double vision, or trouble speaking or swallowing. Examination: wasting of the hand muscles (left more than right), fasciculations in both arms and thighs, weakness of grip and of left ankle dorsiflexion, brisk reflexes with spread and a positive Hoffmann sign, normal sensation. Mixed upper and lower motor neuron signs; evaluation for motor neuron disease and its mimics begun, with neuromuscular neurology consultation booked: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Evaluation of progressive weakness with mixed upper and lower motor neuron signs: blood count, metabolic panel with calcium, creatine kinase, vitamin B12, TSH, A1c, serum protein electrophoresis with immunofixation, and an HIV test; MRI of the brain and cervical spine; seated spirometry. Guideline: Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: multidisciplinary care, symptom management, and cognitive/behavioral impairment (an evidence-based review) (2009); A proposal for new diagnostic criteria for ALS (Gold Coast criteria) (2020); El Escorial revisited: revised criteria for the diagnosis of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (2000) [S]</item><item>Neuromuscular neurology consultation with EMG and nerve conduction studies for progressive weakness with mixed upper and lower motor neuron signs. Guideline: Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: multidisciplinary care, symptom management, and cognitive/behavioral impairment (an evidence-based review) (2009); A proposal for new diagnostic criteria for ALS (Gold Coast criteria) (2020) [S]</item><item>Safety while the evaluation proceeds: no competitive play or heavy lifting, a physical therapy assessment of balance and gait, home fall precautions (night lights, rails, no loose rugs), and a same-day call for any trouble swallowing or breathing; results given to him first, in person. Guideline: Practice parameter update: the care of the patient with amyotrophic lateral sclerosis: multidisciplinary care, symptom management, and cognitive/behavioral impairment (an evidence-based review) (2009) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
